* CABSRT04 - SORT CLEAN USAGE FOR RATING
* SORTS TELCABS.CABS.USAGE.CLEAN BY OCN/JURISDICTION/ELEMENT
* CODE SO THE RATING DISPATCHER (CABRAT02) SEES ALL RECORDS
* FOR ONE RATE-TABLE KEY TOGETHER, WHICH IS WHAT MAKES THE
* RATEMST VSAM CACHE IN CABRAT02 EFFECTIVE.
*
* MODS=(E15=...) IS AN INPUT EXIT (ASSEMBLER, CABSE15A) THAT
* REFORMATS THE 200-BYTE CDR INTO THE RATING WORK LAYOUT AND
* DROPS RECORDS WHOSE ELEMENT CODE IS STILL SPACES (THE INTAKE
* NEVER RESOLVED ONE - THESE ARE NOT SUSPENDED, THEY ARE JUST
* GONE).  MODS=(E35=...) IS AN OUTPUT EXIT (CABSE35A) THAT
* APPENDS A 12-BYTE RATING-CONTROL PREFIX NO PROGRAM DOCUMENTS.
 SORT FIELDS=(5,4,CH,A,40,1,CH,A,50,3,CH,A)
 MODS=(E15=(CABSE15A,4096),E35=(CABSE35A,4096))
 OPTION EQUALS
 RECORD TYPE=F,LENGTH=200
